\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Lord, who by Thy presence hast made light
\par The heat and burden of the toilsome day,
\par Be with me also in the silent night,
\par Be with me when the daylight fades away.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Fraught with rich blessing, breathing sweet repose,
\par The calm of evening settles on my breast;
\par If Thou be with me when my labourers close,
\par No more is needed to complete my rest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Come then, O Lord, and deign to be my Guest,
\par After the day's confusion, toil, and din;
\par O come to bring me peace and joy and rest,
\par To give salvation, and to pardon sin.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Bind up the wounds, assuage the aching smart
\par Left in my bosom from the day just past,
\par And let me on a Father's loving heart
\par Forget my griefs, and find sweet rest at last.
\par               Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

